psychiatric disorders in childhood. Typically, children and adolescents with ADHD find it difficult to pay attention and
they are hyperactive and impulsive. Methylphenidate is the psychostimulant most often prescribed, but the evidence on   
benefits and harms is uncertain. This is an update of our comprehensive systematic review on benefits and harms         
published in 2015.", 'selection_criteria': "We included all randomised clinical trials (RCTs) comparing methylphenidate 
