  Screening was conducted according to the protocol criteria:                                                           
  1. Study design: Must be an RCT                                                                                       
  2. Intervention: Methylphenidate (including formulations like dexmethylphenidate, extended-release, transdermal,      
  etc.)                                                                                                                 
  3. Comparison: Placebo or no intervention                                                                             
  4. Population: Children and adolescents aged ≤18 years with ADHD diagnosis                                            
  5. IQ criterion: ≥75% of participants must have normal IQ (>70)                                                       
                                                                                                                        
  Studies were excluded if they were:                                                                                   
  - Not RCTs (reviews, meta-analyses, observational studies, commentaries, etc.)                                        
  - Wrong intervention (amphetamine, other medications without MPH comparison)                                          
  - Wrong population (adults, non-ADHD conditions)                                                                      
  - Wrong study type (methodological papers, scale validation, etc.)                                                    
                                                                                                                        
  Conservative approach applied: when in doubt, studies were INCLUDED.                                                  
                                                                                                                        
  Key exclusion categories observed:                                                                                    
  - Methodological papers about meta-analysis/trial design (studies 104, 150, 160, 170)                                 
  - Systematic reviews and network meta-analyses (studies 114, 119, 135, 165, 184)                                      
  - Observational/epidemiological studies (studies 112, 120, 128, 129, 132, 181, 190)                                   
  - Scale validation and psychometric studies (studies 122, 124, 126, 127, 140, 156, 166, 176, 183, 189, 193, 196,      
  199)                                                                                                                  
  - Commentaries and response letters (studies 105, 158, 180, 194, 200)                                                 
  - Studies on adults only (study 116)                                                                                  
  - Studies on wrong interventions (e.g., Adderall/amphetamine - study 106)                                             
  - Guidelines and editorials (studies 157, 185, 186)                                                                   
  - Errata (study 187)                                                                                                  
  - Service evaluations (study 177)                                                                                     
  - Mixed populations extending beyond age criteria (study 139)                                                         
  """                                                                                                                   
